🚨🇺🇸 A landmark case series published in the Journal Medical Acupuncture evaluated the effectiveness of a specialized ear acupuncture method called Soliman Auricular Allergy Treatment (SAAT) for managing alpha-gal syndrome (AGS). The study tracked 137 patients diagnosed with the tick-borne read meat allergy across two clinical sites in the U.S. Out of the 126 patients with available follow-up data, an astonishing 121 individuals (96%) reported complete clinical remission of their symptoms. This allowed the vast majority of individuals to safely reintroduce mammalian meat and dairy products back into their diets without experiencing the delayed, severe gastrointestinal or dermatological allergic reactions typical of AGS. 
